From 5dccb8edcec5e37be052082e7afe94804d54fab4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CosmosEx Buildroot <4372835+planeturban@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:48:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ce_main_app: settings API section for /pi sharing (NFS and
 SMB)

GET/PUT /api/v1/settings/pishare: whether /pi is shared over NFS and SMB,
read-write or read-only, which computers may connect (addresses,
networks a.b.c.d/n, host names or *; at most 16), NFS file ownership
(all clients as the user pi, or their own user ids), SMB guest access
or the user pi with a password (set with "password", reported as
"passwordSet", never returned), the SMB workgroup; plus whether the
servers run and what NFS shares now. Settings go to /etc/ce-pishare.conf
(temp file, sync, rename) and are applied with the image's
/usr/sbin/ce-pishare; without that tool the section says "available":
false. Image-specific (Buildroot image).
---
